# Cloudflare Pages redirects
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# Format: <from> <to> <status>
# Cloudflare Pages already serves /articles/foo for /articles/foo.html
# automatically, so we only need the trailing-slash rewrite for old links
# that the wild has indexed with the slash.

/articles/*/  /articles/:splat.html  200
/categories/*/  /categories/:splat.html  200
/guides  /guides.html  200
/guides/  /guides.html  200
/search  /search.html  200
/search/  /search.html  200

# www -> apex 301 is handled by functions/_middleware.js because the
# Cloudflare Pages _redirects format only supports path-based sources, not
# full URLs. The middleware runs on every request and 301s www host to apex.
